# Compose files are host-side tooling only - never needed inside the image
# (M006 Round 6, PID §15/§D). This specifically closes a real gap found
# during this round: an untracked, machine-local docker-compose.override.yml
# (LiteLLM secret-*path* bind fragment - not a secret value itself, but
# still local machine config that must not enter the release artifact) was
# NOT previously excluded here, so a build from a working tree that had one
# present would silently copy it into the image via `COPY . .`. Broadened
# to every docker-compose*.yml (covers docker-compose.yml and
# docker-compose.release.yml too - neither has any runtime purpose inside
# the image) rather than naming only the one file that happened to exist
# locally at audit time.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
# Backup archives / restore output - large, binary, never part of the app.
backups/
